<article class="env-lemma" id="07ZQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07ZQ">Lemma <span data-tag="07ZQ">28.25.7</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated morphism of schemes. Let $Z \subset Y$ be a closed subset such that $Y \setminus Z$ is retrocompact in $Y$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Let $\mathcal{F}' \subset \mathcal{F}$ be the subsheaf of sections supported in $f^{-1}Z$. Then $f_*\mathcal{F}' \subset f_*\mathcal{F}$ is the subsheaf of sections supported in $Z$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. (Hint: First show that $X \setminus f^{-1}Z$ is retrocompact in $X$ as $Y \setminus Z$ is retrocompact in $Y$. Hence Lemma <a href="/tag/07ZP" data-tag="07ZP">28.25.5</a> applies to $f^{-1}Z$ and $\mathcal{F}$. As $f$ is quasi-compact and quasi-separated we see that $f_*\mathcal{F}$ is quasi-coherent. Hence Lemma <a href="/tag/07ZP" data-tag="07ZP">28.25.5</a> applies to $Z$ and $f_*\mathcal{F}$. Finally, match the sheaves directly.) 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>